# Input graph for test_structure_round_trip, passed through demo(fixture=...).
# The 'down' path from PAPER is complete, but its sentence has NO up-link;
# another sentence, in another paragraph and section, has both. The original
# fails at the second assertion ('cannot walk back up'). Widening the
# interpolated {rdflib.URIRef(sent)} to a variable finds the other sentence:
# with both occurrences widened to one variable it fails later (u_para !=
# para); with only the subject of prov:wasQuotedFrom widened it passes.
@base <https://kumagallium.github.io/asterism/papers/resource/> .
@prefix po: <http://www.essepuntato.it/2008/12/pattern#> .
@prefix doco: <http://purl.org/spar/doco/> .
@prefix nif: <http://persistence.uni-leipzig.de/nlp2rdf/ontologies/nif-core#> .
@prefix prov: <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#> .
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .

<paper/PMC5951533> po:contains <sec/1> .
<sec/1> a doco:Section ; po:contains <para/1> .
<para/1> a doco:Paragraph ; po:contains <sent/1> .
<sent/1> a doco:Sentence .

<sec/Y> po:contains <para/Y> .
<para/Y> po:contains <sent/Y> .
<sent/Y> prov:wasQuotedFrom <paper/PMC5951533> ;
    nif:referenceContext <paper/PMC5951533/fulltext> .
